From ebf1ed5a6a30947e677e3134b16731c11b950bb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:39:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Availability: PIF in-app categories, exclusions list layout,
 schedule-from-menu

- Pay It Forward eligible-categories now lists only categories that appear in
  the app menu (hides the extra Square categories); any already-selected
  category stays shown so it can still be turned off.
- Day exclusions rebuilt with the Sold-out layout: category chips + a
  search-as-you-type list of the offered (Product Builder) menu items, each with
  an Available / Sold out toggle for the selected day, keyed by the menu id so it
  takes effect on the customer menu.
- Menu schedules can be seeded from an existing menu: a row of one-tap chips (one
  per existing menu/category/section) creates a schedule pre-named and
  pre-selected for that menu, alongside the existing '+ New custom menu schedule'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0187Jj4Q77V4UPawzEh9gsGr
